#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:76
msgid "List triggers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:77
msgid "Lists every trigger (site event) Notification Master can react to, grouped the way the admin screen groups them: one group per enabled post type, taxonomy and comment type, plus media, user, theme, plugin and privacy, and the WooCommerce order, product and review groups only when Notification Master Pro is licensed and WooCommerce is active. Each trigger carries its slug (the exact value a notification stores), the merge-tag groups its content may use, how many notifications currently use it (notifications_active = published and firing, notifications_draft = disabled) and whether it is a Pro trigger. A trigger family switched off in the settings is absent here even if notifications still reference it; list-notifications reports that as trigger_active false. Pass group to narrow the list to one group slug; an unknown group returns an empty triggers list while the groups map always names every valid slug. Changes nothing. Read-only, so the run endpoint is a GET with bracket-encoded input: ?input[group]=post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:84
msgid "Return only the triggers in this group slug, e.g. \"post\", \"page\", \"comment\", \"user\". Omit for every group."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:96
msgid "Every trigger group on this site, keyed by group slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:195
msgid "List merge tags"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:196
msgid "Lists the merge tags a notification on the given trigger may use in its subject, message, URL or body, written as {{group.key}}, for example {{post.title}} or {{general.blogname}}. Groups come back keyed by group slug with the shared \"general\" group first. Each group has a label, is_advanced, available (advanced groups such as ACF fields need Notification Master Pro, so available is false for them on the free plan), the plugin the group depends on (null when none) and whether that plugin is active, and its tags keyed by tag key with label, description and type (null when untyped; \"datetime\" tags can drive a connection schedule). The trigger slug is checked here: an unknown slug answers 400 ntfm_invalid_trigger with the allowed slugs, and a Pro WooCommerce trigger on the free plan answers 403 ntfm_pro_required. Changes nothing. Read-only, so the run endpoint is a GET with bracket-encoded input: ?input[trigger]=post-published."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:203
msgid "Trigger slug exactly as list-triggers reports it, e.g. \"post-published\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:215
msgid "Merge-tag groups keyed by slug, \"general\" first. Each is {label, is_advanced, available, depends_on_plugin, plugin_dependency_active, merge_tags: {key: {label, description, type}}}."
msgstr ""

