msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:305
msgid "List channels"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:306
msgid "Lists the delivery channels (integrations) a notification connection can use. The free plugin ships webpush, email, webhook, discord and instagram; facebook, twitterx, twilio, slack, zapier, make and whatsapp need Notification Master Pro and on the free plan are listed with available false and requires \"Notification Master Pro\", so an agent can tell a locked channel from an unknown one. Each channel reports its connection settings keys, which of those hold credentials or recipient lists (secret_keys: always redacted elsewhere and never writable through update-notification), whether it is configured where that is knowable (webpush: both VAPID keys set; instagram: an account connected; null for channels configured per connection) and how many connections across the first 100 notifications use it and how many of those are enabled. Never returns a credential. Takes no input. Read-only, so the run endpoint is a GET; with no input the bracket-encoded query string (?input[...]) stays empty."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: channel name
#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:393
#, php-format
msgid "Send notifications to %s. Available in Notification Master Pro."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:427
msgid "List starter templates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:428
msgid "Lists the ready-made starter notifications that notification-master/create-notification-from-template can import: one per registered trigger, each pre-wired with an email and a web push connection (enabled) plus discord, webhook and instagram shells (disabled). Returns each template id (pass it as template_id), title, trigger slug, group label, whether that trigger is registered right now, and one {id, integration, enabled} summary per connection. HTML bodies and connection settings are left out on purpose; import a template and read it with get-notification to see them. Pass group to narrow the list to one trigger group slug such as \"post\" or \"user\". Changes nothing. Read-only, so the run endpoint is a GET with bracket-encoded input: ?input[group]=post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:435
msgid "Return only templates whose trigger belongs to this group slug. Omit for every group."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:549
msgid "Get settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-catalog-abilities.php:550
msgid "Reads the Notification Master settings merged over their defaults: which trigger families are on (post_status_change_trigger, taxonomy_term_change_trigger, comment_change_trigger, user_change_trigger, theme_change_trigger, plugin_change_trigger, media_change_trigger, privacy_trigger and, only when Pro is licensed, woocommerce_change_trigger), which post types, taxonomies and comment types fire triggers, log retention in days (delete_logs_every for the debug log, notifications_delete_logs_every for the send log), whether background processing is on, and the web push subscribe-button appearance options. The VAPID key pair is never returned; webpush_configured says whether both keys are set. is_pro says whether Notification Master Pro is licensed. There is deliberately no write counterpart: changing these re-registers triggers and can silently stop live notifications, so it stays a human decision in wp-admin. Takes no input. Read-only, so the run endpoint is a GET; with no input the bracket-encoded query string (?input[...]) stays empty."
msgstr ""

