#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:92
msgid "List scheduled sends"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:93
msgid "Lists the per-connection sends Notification Master has queued in Action Scheduler, one row per pending (or, with status, completed or failed) action: the notification and connection it belongs to, the channel, the trigger that queued it, and the fire time both as a UNIX timestamp (scheduled_for, 0 when unknown) and as a GMT datetime (scheduled_for_gmt). This is the same list the REST route GET /ntfm/v1/scheduled serves. Pass notification_id to see only one notification's sends; the filter runs in the database, so paging is exact. It reads only and never changes a schedule; use notification-master/cancel-scheduled-send to remove one. Cancelled actions are removed by Action Scheduler's cleaner on a later queue run, so they drop out of this list; the send log (notification-master/list-send-log) is the durable record of what was delivered. Because this ability is read-only its run endpoint is a GET and the input is read from the query string, so bracket-encode it: ?input[status]=pending&input[per_page]=50."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:101
msgid "Action status to list. Defaults to pending, the sends that have not fired yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:106
msgid "Return only sends belonging to this notification."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:111
#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:217
#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:475
#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:111
msgid "Page of results to return. Defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:117
msgid "Rows per page, 1 to 100. Defaults to 20."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:195
msgid "List send log"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:196
msgid "Lists Notification Master's send log, newest first: one row per delivery attempt with the channel (integration), whether it succeeded (\"success\") or failed (\"error\"), the notification and trigger it came from, the integration's own result message and, for HTTP channels, the response code or error text in detail. Filter by status, integration slug or a substring of the notification name; total counts every row matching the filters so a caller can page. This is the right place to answer \"did it go out\" and \"why did it fail\". It never returns the raw log content: recipient email addresses, webhook URLs, headers and credentials are stripped, and any email address left inside a message is masked as [email]. Because this ability is read-only its run endpoint is a GET and the input is read from the query string, so bracket-encode it: ?input[status]=error&input[per_page]=50."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:204
msgid "Return only successful or only failed sends. Omit for both."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:208
msgid "Channel slug such as email, webpush, webhook, discord or instagram. See notification-master/list-channels."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:212
msgid "Exact match on the notification name recorded with the send."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:223
#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:481
#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:117
msgid "Rows per page, 1 to 100. Defaults to 25."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:242
msgid "\"success\" or \"error\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:249
msgid "The integration's result message, with email addresses masked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:253
msgid "HTTP response code and message, or the error text, when the integration recorded one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:316
msgid "Get send stats"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:317
msgid "Counts Notification Master's sends over the last N days (1 to 30, default 7) without returning a single log row: overall total, success and failed counts, a daily series with exactly one entry per requested day (days with no sends are present with zeros), and the same split per channel in by_integration. Use it to spot a channel that started failing or a day with no deliveries. Dates use the site timezone because the log rows were written with current_time(); the from/to values show the exact window counted. Runs two grouped queries regardless of log size. Because this ability is read-only its run endpoint is a GET and the input is read from the query string, so bracket-encode it: ?input[days]=14."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:326
msgid "How many days back to count, today included. Defaults to 7."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:457
msgid "List debug log"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:458
msgid "Lists Notification Master's internal debug log, newest first. Unlike the send log, these rows are written by the plugin itself: a scheduled send that was dropped (action \"scheduling\", with the reason, e.g. notification_missing or connection_disabled, surfaced as summary), an unknown integration slug (\"invalid_integration\"), and other errors, info and debug notes. Filter by type (error, info, debug) or by the exact action string. content is the recorded context with credentials, endpoints, IP addresses and user agents replaced by [redacted] and email addresses masked; date may be null on old rows. It changes nothing. Because this ability is read-only its run endpoint is a GET and the input is read from the query string, so bracket-encode it: ?input[type]=error&input[per_page]=50."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:466
msgid "Return only rows of this level. Omit for all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:470
msgid "Exact action string, e.g. scheduling or invalid_integration."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:499
msgid "error, info or debug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:504
msgid "The drop reason for scheduling rows, otherwise the action."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:568
msgid "Get subscriber stats"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:569
msgid "Counts the site's web push subscribers: total, subscribed and unsubscribed, a split by device (desktop, mobile, tablet, unknown), a split by browser (chrome, firefox, safari, opera, other) and how many subscribed in the last 7 days, plus push_configured, which is false until VAPID keys are saved in Notification Master settings. It returns counts only: no subscription rows, endpoints, keys, IP addresses or user agents ever leave this ability, and there is no ability to list, delete or unsubscribe subscribers. Takes no input. Read-only, so the run endpoint is a GET."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:649
msgid "Cancel scheduled send"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:650
msgid "Cancels one pending scheduled send so it never fires. Takes the action_id from notification-master/list-scheduled-sends and removes that Action Scheduler action; the notification itself, its connections and its schedule settings are untouched, so the next real trigger event schedules a fresh send as usual. Only a pending Notification Master send can be cancelled: an action_id that is missing, already complete, failed, cancelled, or that belongs to another plugin answers 404 ntfm_scheduled_send_not_found. Nothing is sent and no log row is written. The cancelled row keeps status canceled only until Action Scheduler's cleaner removes it on a later queue run, so do not rely on list-scheduled-sends as an audit trail; the send log is the durable record. The response repeats what was cancelled, including was_scheduled_for, so the caller can confirm it hit the intended send."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:658
#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:730
msgid "Action Scheduler action ID of the pending send, from notification-master/list-scheduled-sends."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:670
msgid "Always true: the send is no longer queued."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:677
msgid "UNIX timestamp the send would have fired at, 0 when unknown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:721
msgid "Send scheduled now"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:722
msgid "Delivers one pending scheduled send immediately instead of at its scheduled time. THIS SENDS FOR REAL: depending on the connection it emails the configured recipients, pushes to subscribers, posts to Discord or a webhook, or publishes to Instagram, exactly as the scheduled run would have. It is synchronous and blocks on the outbound HTTP call (Instagram can take up to 60 seconds), and the Action Scheduler row is cancelled before dispatch and marked complete afterwards with the log line \"Sent immediately via send-now\", so a timed-out request may still have delivered and list-scheduled-sends with status complete then shows it. Requires confirm set to true and confirm_action_id equal to action_id; a mismatch answers 400 ntfm_confirm_mismatch before anything is looked up. An action_id that is not a pending Notification Master send answers 404 ntfm_scheduled_send_not_found. The delivery result is written to the send log, not returned here: read notification-master/list-send-log afterwards. This ability is not available over MCP (meta.mcp.public is false); it runs only through the REST /run endpoint or PHP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:735
msgid "Must be true. Confirms a human accepted that this delivers to real recipients now."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:740
msgid "Must repeat action_id exactly. Guards against sending the wrong queued action."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:752
msgid "Always true: the send was handed to the integration."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:772
msgid "confirm must be true and confirm_action_id must equal action_id. Nothing was sent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:775
msgid "confirm_action_id must repeat action_id exactly; this delivers to real recipients."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:885
#: includes/scheduling/class-scheduler.php:446
#: includes/scheduling/class-scheduler.php:460
msgid "No pending scheduled send with that action_id."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:888
msgid "It may have already run or been cancelled."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:908
#: includes/scheduling/class-scheduler.php:467
msgid "The queue is delivering this scheduled send right now. Nothing was sent twice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:911
msgid "The queue runner delivers it once. Check notification-master/list-send-log in a moment."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:941
msgid "UNIX timestamp of the fire time, 0 when unknown."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-delivery-abilities.php:945
msgid "Fire time as a GMT datetime, null when scheduled_for is 0."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:93
msgid "List notifications"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:94
msgid "Lists notifications one page at a time, newest first, each with its status, trigger and the connections (channels) it sends through. It never returns connection settings: no recipients, no webhook URLs, no credentials and no message bodies. Use notification-master/get-notification for one notification's redacted settings. \"enabled\" is true when the status is publish, which means the notification fires on its trigger and sends to real recipients. \"trigger_active\" is false when the stored trigger is not registered on this site (its family is disabled in settings or it needs Notification Master Pro), and such a notification never fires. \"total\" counts every notification matching the status and trigger filters, not only this page. Because this ability is read-only its run endpoint is a GET and the input is read from the query string, so bracket-encode it: ?input[status]=publish&input[page]=2&input[per_page]=50."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:102
msgid "publish returns enabled notifications, draft returns disabled ones, any returns both. Defaults to any."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:106
msgid "Return only notifications on this trigger slug, e.g. post-published. Slugs come from notification-master/list-triggers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:133
msgid "Notifications matching the filters across all pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:168
msgid "Pass a slug from the allowed list, or omit trigger to list every notification."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:236
msgid "Merge tag group slugs the trigger offers, \"general\" first. Empty when the trigger is not registered. Read the tags themselves with notification-master/list-merge-tags."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:240
msgid "Delayed sends queued for this notification and not yet delivered (pending Action Scheduler rows, counted in one query)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:246
msgid "Get notification"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:247
msgid "Returns one notification: the same row notification-master/list-notifications shows, plus each connection's settings and schedule, the merge tag groups its trigger offers and how many delayed sends are still queued for it. Settings are redacted before they leave the site: recipient lists, webhook URLs, headers and API credentials come back as \"[redacted]\" or \"[redacted: N items]\" so the agent can tell an empty list from a filled one without reading it. Text settings such as subject, title and message stay readable, so this is where to look before notification-master/update-notification. \"schedule\" carries the stored delay or merge-tag-relative config together with a one-line \"summary\"; summary is null when the connection sends immediately. Because this ability is read-only its run endpoint is a GET and the input is read from the query string, so bracket-encode it: ?input[id]=12."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:255
#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:316
#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:434
msgid "Notification id from notification-master/list-notifications."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:307
msgid "Set notification status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:308
msgid "Enables a notification by setting it to publish, or disables it by setting it to draft. Enabling makes it fire on the next real event and send to real recipients; disabling also drops already-queued delayed sends at fire time. Nothing is sent by this call itself. Idempotent: asking for the status it already has returns changed false and writes nothing. \"pending_scheduled_sends\" reports how many delayed sends are queued for it so a human can judge what disabling will drop, or what enabling will let through."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:321
msgid "publish enables the notification, draft disables it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:342
msgid "False when the notification already had the requested status."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: editable settings keys per channel, 2: channel slugs the free plugin ships
#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:422
#, php-format
msgid "Renames a notification and/or edits its existing connections: toggle a connection on or off, rename it, or change its text settings. Only content keys are editable and the allowed keys per channel are %1$s. Recipients, URLs, headers, credentials and the Pro-only condition keys are refused with ntfm_invalid_setting; change those in wp-admin. Discord's message is an object (title, description, content, author, fields) and webhook's body is a list of {key, value} pairs; each replaces the stored value whole. Supplied settings are merged over the stored ones and the result is validated against the channel's own schema before anything is written, so a refusal means nothing changed. Connection ids come from notification-master/get-notification; an unknown id is refused with ntfm_connection_not_found and the valid ids. New connections cannot be added here. Connections on Pro-only channels (slack, twilio, whatsapp, zapier, make, facebook, twitterx) are refused with ntfm_pro_required on the free plan; with Notification Master Pro active their listed content keys are editable like any other. The channels this plugin ships are %2$s. Writing does not send anything, but an enabled notification uses the new text on its next real event."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:425
msgid "Update notification"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:440
msgid "New notification name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:444
msgid "Patches keyed by connection id. Each may set enabled, name and/or settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:450
msgid "Whether this connection sends when the notification fires."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:454
msgid "New connection name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:458
msgid "Text settings to merge over the stored ones. Only the channel's content keys are accepted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:481
msgid "Dotted paths whose stored value actually changed, e.g. name or connections.email_default.settings.subject. Empty when every supplied value already matched."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:523
msgid "Neither a name nor a connection change was supplied."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:541
msgid "The notification name cannot be empty."
msgstr ""

